{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79iPE8d6oPXQZEG7jLj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017LNbmzwmucKLMH4zCvo315","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":340,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3243,"cache_read_input_tokens":196121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3243},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28ffd53f-5e6f-4890-9e75-d2c49ec7ad63","uuid":"2145f6fd-e678-44be-a399-b68440253771","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:22:14.609Z","request_id":"req_011Ch79iP1zFhXdEKkhh11hG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017LNbmzwmucKLMH4zCvo315":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":340,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LNbmzwmucKLMH4zCvo315","type":"tool_result","content":"340\t- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n341\t  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n342\t- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n343\t  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n344\t  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n345\t  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n346\t  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n347\t\n348\t### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n349\t\n350\t- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n351\t  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n352\t  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n353\t- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n354\t  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n355\t  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n356\t- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n357\t  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n358\t- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n359\t  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`\n360\t    on Python 3.13 and later, so a baseline recorded on 3.9 to 3.12 no\n361\t    longer reads as phantom sites on 3.13 and 3.14. The push run of\n362\t    `validate.yml` has no 3.14 leg; the scheduled run on that commit\n363\t    passed on 2026-11-03, its Python 3.14 leg included.\n364\t  - The ownership e2e check C.3 finds the canonical guards through the\n365\t    `--is-canonical` oracle, with a never-canonical negative control,\n366\t    instead of grepping the hook text.\n367\t- The Coverage job's timeout rises from 35 to 50 minutes. The scheduled\n368\t  job ran 34 min 36 s on 2026-11-02 and was cancelled at 35 min 05 s on\n369\t  2026-11-03, and a cancelled run on `HEAD` blocks the release preflight.\n370\t- `REVIEW.md` is added to the framework repository, and its existing\n371\t  pull-request template gains prompts for the literal output of the test\n372\t  plan, for the canonical or kernel files touched, and for how to revert.\n373\t\n374\t### Known-open (declared by this release)\n375\t\n376\t- **The Tier-1 coverage gate and the `mcp-smoke.yml` path filters still\n377\t  name only the entry points.** The coverage gate measures the entry-point\n378\t  files, not the packages that hold the logic. The `mcp-smoke.yml` push and\n379\t  pull-request filters name the entry points, not the split's packages;\n380\t  its daily scheduled run still runs. No release is assigned to its cure\n381\t  yet.\n382\t- **The pair-rail inputs-hash manifest lists the entry points only.** The\n383\t  inputs hash that the release workflow recomputes does not cover the\n384\t  packages behind them. No release is assigned to its cure yet.\n385\t- **The VETO floor admits retired ids** (Security and governance, above).\n386\t  No release is assigned to its cure yet.\n387\t- **The model allowlist admits other vendors' ids and retired ids**\n388\t  (Security and governance, above). The settings-tamper detector\n389\t  (`settings_tamper_model_remap`), the agent `model:` check and the\n390\t  tier-policy loader no longer flag an id of the admitted families,\n391\t  Gemini, Grok and retired Claude 4 ids among them. No release is assigned\n392\t  to its cure yet.\n393\t- **The Codex pin.** A newer Codex CLI passes on its declared version\n394\t  alone, the pin file's floor and the ADR-182 amendment disagree, and the\n395\t  verdict validator does not bind a declared version to its payload hash.\n396\t  The hook fixtures for Codex as a hook host still date from 0.139.0. No\n397\t  release is assigned to its cure yet.\n398\t- **Files merged without the signing ceremony.** The 233 canonical paths\n399\t  that pull requests #6 and #7 brought, the kernel paths among them, are"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28ffd53f-5e6f-4890-9e75-d2c49ec7ad63","uuid":"9c5eab35-23ee-43a5-8de8-6bd8395cd7e4","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:22:14.638Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n\n### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n\n- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`\n    on Python 3.13 and later, so a baseline recorded on 3.9 to 3.12 no\n    longer reads as phantom sites on 3.13 and 3.14. The push run of\n    `validate.yml` has no 3.14 leg; the scheduled run on that commit\n    passed on 2026-11-03, its Python 3.14 leg included.\n  - The ownership e2e check C.3 finds the canonical guards through the\n    `--is-canonical` oracle, with a never-canonical negative control,\n    instead of grepping the hook text.\n- The Coverage job's timeout rises from 35 to 50 minutes. The scheduled\n  job ran 34 min 36 s on 2026-11-02 and was cancelled at 35 min 05 s on\n  2026-11-03, and a cancelled run on `HEAD` blocks the release preflight.\n- `REVIEW.md` is added to the framework repository, and its existing\n  pull-request template gains prompts for the literal output of the test\n  plan, for the canonical or kernel files touched, and for how to revert.\n\n### Known-open (declared by this release)\n\n- **The Tier-1 coverage gate and the `mcp-smoke.yml` path filters still\n  name only the entry points.** The coverage gate measures the entry-point\n  files, not the packages that hold the logic. The `mcp-smoke.yml` push and\n  pull-request filters name the entry points, not the split's packages;\n  its daily scheduled run still runs. No release is assigned to its cure\n  yet.\n- **The pair-rail inputs-hash manifest lists the entry points only.** The\n  inputs hash that the release workflow recomputes does not cover the\n  packages behind them. No release is assigned to its cure yet.\n- **The VETO floor admits retired ids** (Security and governance, above).\n  No release is assigned to its cure yet.\n- **The model allowlist admits other vendors' ids and retired ids**\n  (Security and governance, above). The settings-tamper detector\n  (`settings_tamper_model_remap`), the agent `model:` check and the\n  tier-policy loader no longer flag an id of the admitted families,\n  Gemini, Grok and retired Claude 4 ids among them. No release is assigned\n  to its cure yet.\n- **The Codex pin.** A newer Codex CLI passes on its declared version\n  alone, the pin file's floor and the ADR-182 amendment disagree, and the\n  verdict validator does not bind a declared version to its payload hash.\n  The hook fixtures for Codex as a hook host still date from 0.139.0. No\n  release is assigned to its cure yet.\n- **Files merged without the signing ceremony.** The 233 canonical paths\n  that pull requests #6 and #7 brought, the kernel paths among them, are","numLines":60,"startLine":340,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017LNbmzwmucKLMH4zCvo315","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
